    "result_text": "All three findings addressed, tests green (`BUILD SUCCESS`, 1 test, 0 failures). I agreed with all three \u2014 they're pure structural cleanups.\n\n**What I changed:**\n\n1. **Duplicated domain extraction (`EmailDomainValidator`)** \u2014 Extracted a shared `private static String domainOf(String email)` (returns the lower-cased domain, or `null` when absent). Both `isValid` and `isDisposableAdjacent` now call it, so the `@`-parsing and boundary check live once. `isValid` collapsed to a one-liner.\n\n2. **Soft-capacity magic number (`OwnerRestControllerV1`)** \u2014 Added `SOFT_CAPACITY = 40` and `HARD_CAPACITY = 50` constants. `isApproachingCapacity` now reads `count >= SOFT_CAPACITY && count < HARD_CAPACITY`, `isOverSoftCapacity` reads `count >= SOFT_CAPACITY`, and the create-time hard rejection in `addOwner` uses `>= HARD_CAPACITY`. The boundary is expressed once and shared across all three related predicates.\n\n3. **Idiom nit** \u2014 Replaced the inline fully-qualified `java.util.stream.Collectors.toUnmodifiableSet()` with a normal `import java.util.stream.Collectors;` matching the file's style.\n\nNone of these alter behaviour \u2014 the acceptance test still passes and the create-time capacity semantics are unchanged (`>= 50` \u2192 `>= HARD_CAPACITY`, `40..49` \u2192 `>= SOFT_CAPACITY && < HARD_CAPACITY`).",
